or offering HTTP/HTTPS as a segmented control or dropdown rather than a plain text field.\n\nFor the connectivity status, I'm worried the baseline renders \"用户云服务状态: 正常\" as a single concatenated text span rather than separate label/value components, which would break exact-text matchers looking for just \"正常\" or \"不可用\" — so I'm recommending the status value be split into its own distinct text element.\n\nFor the toast message \"配置已保存，正在检查服务是否可用…\", I'm checking whether hypium exposes a toast-detection utility like a toast listener, since toasts are transient and the test would need to catch it within its short display window.\n\nThe status update after the check should reflect the actual connectivity result, not a faked success, per the FAQ guidance. For URL composition with user/password, since the reference API doesn't natively support auth, I'll lean toward adding Basic Auth credentials to the request config as the sensible default when those fields are populated, consistent with how reverse proxies typically expect it.\n\nFor storage, I should persist the individual fields but also compose them into the existing API_URL key so all other code paths (like getApiUrl) keep working unchanged, with backward-compatible parsing of an existing apiUrl string into fields when the fields themselves aren't present yet. I'm also considering the edge case of an empty host — whether that should mark the config as unconfigured with status unavailable, or still attempt a check that would simply fail.\n\nFor empty port, I should omit it and default to 80/443, with path normalization adding a leading slash and stripping trailing slashes, stripping any scheme the user includes in the host, and trimming whitespace throughout. For the second scenario, the recommendation feed should show a \"set up online service\" prompt and button when the online service isn't configured — likely triggered simply by an empty apiUrl on fresh install, though","startTime":1792255878451,"lastModifiedT